outputs.L1:
A computer-implemented method for access control to a restricted resource of a resource provider in a network-connected computer system, wherein a blockchain data structure accessible via the network stores digitally signed records validated by network-connected miner software components, the method comprising:

identifying an access control role definition for access to the resource, the role including a specification of access permissions;

defining a cryptocurrency for indicating authorization to access the resource, the cryptocurrency comprising tradable units of value associated with records in the blockchain, wherein transfers of the cryptocurrency between records in the blockchain are validated by the miners;

receiving a request from an authenticated resource consumer for authorization to access the resource; and

submitting a blockchain transaction to the miner components to transfer a quantity of cryptocurrency to a consumer record in the blockchain, the transaction including an identification of the role, such that the consumer record identifies that the consumer is authorized to access the resource in accordance with the role definition.

outputs.L2:
A network-connected computer system performs an access-control method for a protected resource supplied by a resource provider. In this system, a blockchain data structure available over the network contains digitally signed entries that are verified by miner software components connected to the network. The method comprises:

- determining an access-control role definition governing use of the resource, where the role specifies the relevant access rights;
- establishing a cryptocurrency to represent permission to access the resource, the cryptocurrency consisting of transferable units of value linked to records on the blockchain, with transfers of the cryptocurrency between blockchain records being validated by the miners;
- obtaining a request from an authenticated consumer of the resource seeking authorization to use the resource; and
- sending a blockchain transaction to the miner components to move an amount of the cryptocurrency to a consumer record on the blockchain, the transaction containing an identifier of the role, so that the consumer record indicates that the consumer is permitted to access the resource according to the role definition.

