Below is a sample **independent patent claim** drafted in a method format:

**1. A computer-implemented method for controlling access to a restricted network resource, the method comprising:**

receiving, by an access control server, a request from a client device to access the restricted network resource;

obtaining, by the access control server, a blockchain address associated with a user of the client device;

querying, by the access control server, a blockchain ledger to determine whether the blockchain address holds one or more cryptocurrency tokens associated with an authorization role;

determining, based at least in part on ownership or control of the one or more cryptocurrency tokens, that the user is assigned the authorization role;

mapping, by the access control server, the authorization role to one or more access permissions for the restricted network resource;

generating, by the access control server, an access decision based on the one or more access permissions;

permitting the client device to access the restricted network resource when the access decision indicates that the authorization role authorizes the requested access; and

denying the client device access to the restricted network resource when the access decision indicates that the authorization role does not authorize the requested access,

wherein the one or more cryptocurrency tokens function as transferable blockchain-based representations of authorization roles for controlling access to the restricted network resource.

1. A computer-implemented method for granting access permissions to an authenticated user, the method comprising:

   receiving, by one or more processors of a resource-provider computing system, a request from a user computing device to access a protected resource;

   authenticating, by the one or more processors, a user associated with the user computing device based at least in part on authentication credentials received from the user computing device;

   determining, by the one or more processors, an access permission to be granted to the authenticated user for the protected resource;

   generating, by the one or more processors, a blockchain transaction configured to transfer an amount of cryptocurrency from a blockchain address associated with the resource-provider computing system to a blockchain address associated with the authenticated user, wherein the blockchain transaction includes data identifying the access permission;

   transmitting, by the one or more processors, the blockchain transaction to a peer-to-peer blockchain network for validation;

   receiving, by the one or more processors, confirmation that the blockchain transaction has been included in a block of a blockchain after validation of the blockchain transaction by one or more miners of the peer-to-peer blockchain network; and

   in response to receiving the confirmation, updating, by the one or more processors, an access-control record to grant the authenticated user the access permission to the protected resource.

1. A computer-implemented method for access control in a networked computer system, the method comprising:

   defining, by one or more processors, a plurality of roles associated with respective access privileges for one or more protected computing resources in the networked computer system;

   storing, in a distributed ledger maintained by a blockchain network, one or more role definition records identifying the plurality of roles and the respective access privileges;

   receiving, at an access control service, a request from a user device to access a protected computing resource;

   determining, by the access control service, whether a blockchain record associated with a user identifier of the user device indicates authorization to access the protected computing resource;

   wherein the blockchain record comprises a token transfer recorded on the distributed ledger, the token transfer being from an authorization-issuing account to an account associated with the user identifier, and wherein the token transfer represents assignment of at least one of the plurality of roles to the user identifier;

   validating, by miner nodes of the blockchain network, the blockchain record by reaching consensus and adding the blockchain record to the distributed ledger;

   verifying, by the access control service, that the blockchain record has been miner-validated and corresponds to a role having an access privilege required for the protected computing resource; and

   in response to verifying that the blockchain record has been miner-validated and corresponds to the required access privilege, granting access by the user device to the protected computing resource,

   wherein absence of the miner-validated blockchain record comprising the token transfer causes the access control service to deny access to the protected computing resource.

1. A computer-implemented method for restricting access to provider resources, the method comprising:

receiving, by an access control system associated with a resource provider, an access request from a consumer device for access to a provider resource;

identifying, by the access control system, a consumer identifier associated with the access request;

retrieving, from a blockchain network, one or more digitally signed blockchain records associated with the consumer identifier, the one or more digitally signed blockchain records specifying at least one consumer authorization role and being signed by a private key of an authorized issuer;

verifying, by the access control system, a digital signature of the one or more digitally signed blockchain records using a public key associated with the authorized issuer;

determining, by the access control system, a cryptocurrency balance associated with a blockchain address linked to the consumer identifier;

mapping, by the access control system, the at least one consumer authorization role and the cryptocurrency balance to an access policy for the provider resource, wherein the access policy defines a required consumer authorization role and a minimum cryptocurrency balance for accessing the provider resource;

determining, by the access control system, whether the at least one consumer authorization role satisfies the required consumer authorization role and whether the cryptocurrency balance satisfies the minimum cryptocurrency balance; and

in response to determining that the at least one consumer authorization role satisfies the required consumer authorization role and that the cryptocurrency balance satisfies the minimum cryptocurrency balance, granting the consumer device access to the provider resource, and otherwise denying the consumer device access to the provider resource.
